    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my bosch dishwasher is showing an e15 error code on the display. i checked the manual but i'm not really sure what to do to fix the leak sensor or how to actually get the water out from under the base. can u help?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The error code E15 on your Bosch dishwasher indicates that the control board has detected excessive water intake, likely due to a leak in the door gasket, spray arms, or a faulty drain sensor. Before removing the base, ensure the unit is unplugged and the small access screw on the bottom lip is removed to reveal the mounting brackets. You can then carefully lift the dishwasher to extract the sump, but be prepared to catch small components like the switch assembly or hose connections if you miss the proper tool. Contact Bosch support if the drain hose or internal pump fails to clear the trapped water even after your efforts.",
