      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You generally do not need to pull the entire unit out; tilting the dishwasher forward until it rests on its legs allows you to pull the front edge up and access the pump assembly via the bottom panel. For drying, turn the control board off to undervoltage, and roll the internal impeller first in a small towel to strip moisture, then press the button in and exit sequences to dry it out naturally. If these steps work, wipe the external casing and proceed with sealing or reinstalling the drain hose, but call a technician if the sump remains wet after this process.",
